{
  "topic": "Journey to the center of the Earth",
  "language": "en",
  "format": "long",
  "category": "ciencia",
  "title": "JOURNEY to the CENTER of the EARTH: What's Under Your Feet? 🌍",
  "hook": "If you dug a hole straight down under your feet, what would you find at the center of the Earth?",
  "presenter": "perro",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "role": "hook",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ima_core",
      "narration": "If you dug a hole straight down under your feet, what would you find at the center of the Earth?",
      "on_screen_text": "What's at the center?",
      "highlight_words": [
        "center?"
      ],
      "sfx": "impact",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "mit_hook",
      "narration": "The center is about six thousand four hundred kilometers down. Like a cross-continent trip… but straight down.",
      "on_screen_text": "6,400 km down",
      "highlight_words": [
        "6,400"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "and_hook",
      "narration": "I'm Leo, and today we're going down layer by layer to the heart of the planet.",
      "on_screen_text": "Down layer by layer",
      "highlight_words": [
        "layer"
      ],
      "sfx": "pop",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "cue_giant",
      "narration": "The deepest hole we've ever dug is the Kola well in Russia: just over twelve kilometers.",
      "on_screen_text": "The record: 12 km",
      "highlight_words": [
        "12"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "The crust"
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "cue_giant",
      "narration": "It sounds like a lot, but it's barely a scratch: it didn't even get through the crust.",
      "on_screen_text": "Barely a scratch",
      "highlight_words": [
        "scratch"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "cue_giant",
      "narration": "It took almost twenty years to drill, and they had to stop because the rock was too hot.",
      "on_screen_text": "Too hot to continue",
      "highlight_words": [
        "hot"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sub_plates",
      "narration": "The crust is the layer of rock we live on. Under the oceans it's just a few kilometers thick, under mountains, tens.",
      "on_screen_text": "The crust",
      "highlight_words": [
        "crust"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s8",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sub_plates",
      "narration": "If Earth were an apple, the crust would be thinner than its skin.",
      "on_screen_text": "Thinner than an apple skin",
      "highlight_words": [
        "skin"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s9",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sub_push",
      "narration": "And it's broken into plates that move a few centimeters a year, like the Nazca plate off South America.",
      "on_screen_text": "Moving plates",
      "highlight_words": [
        "plates"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s10",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sub_melt",
      "narration": "Below is the mantle: very hot rock that slowly flows like a paste over millions of years.",
      "on_screen_text": "The mantle",
      "highlight_words": [
        "mantle"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "The mantle"
    },
    {
      "id": "s11",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sub_melt",
      "narration": "The mantle is the thickest layer: almost three thousand kilometers of hot rock.",
      "on_screen_text": "The thickest layer",
      "highlight_words": [
        "thickest"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s12",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sub_rise",
      "narration": "Where a plate sinks, rock melts and magma rises to feed volcanoes.",
      "on_screen_text": "Magma is born",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Magma"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s13",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sub_rise",
      "narration": "Volcanoes are like windows: the magma they spew tells us what the deep rock is like.",
      "on_screen_text": "Windows into the Earth",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Windows"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s14",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "gal_hotspot",
      "narration": "In other places a column of hot rock rises from deep down. That's how the Galápagos Islands were born.",
      "on_screen_text": "Hotspots",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Hotspots"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s15",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "dia_deep",
      "narration": "About a hundred and fifty kilometers down, heat and pressure are so great that carbon turns into diamond.",
      "on_screen_text": "A diamond factory",
      "highlight_words": [
        "diamond"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s16",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "dia_pipe",
      "narration": "Some ride up to the surface in deep, very fast volcanic eruptions.",
      "on_screen_text": "They ride eruptions",
      "highlight_words": [
        "eruptions"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s17",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ima_core",
      "narration": "Further down, almost three thousand kilometers deep, the core begins: a huge ball of iron and nickel.",
      "on_screen_text": "The iron core",
      "highlight_words": [
        "iron"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "The core"
    },
    {
      "id": "s18",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ima_north",
      "narration": "Its outer part is liquid, and as it moves it creates the magnetic field that makes compasses work.",
      "on_screen_text": "Moving liquid iron",
      "highlight_words": [
        "liquid"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s19",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "aur_shield",
      "narration": "That field shields us from particles from the Sun and, near the poles, creates the auroras.",
      "on_screen_text": "Our shield",
      "highlight_words": [
        "shield"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s20",
      "role": "surprise",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sol_surface",
      "narration": "And at the center, the temperature reaches about five thousand four hundred degrees: similar to the surface of the Sun.",
      "on_screen_text": "As hot as the Sun",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Sun"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s21",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ima_core",
      "narration": "But the inner core is solid. The pressure is so enormous that the iron can't melt.",
      "on_screen_text": "Solid from pressure",
      "highlight_words": [
        "pressure"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s22",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "hue_womb",
      "narration": "How do we know, if nobody has been there? By listening to earthquakes.",
      "on_screen_text": "How do we know?",
      "highlight_words": [
        "know?"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s23",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_quake",
      "narration": "Earthquake waves travel through the planet and change speed and direction as they cross each layer.",
      "on_screen_text": "Waves passing through",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Waves"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut",
      "chapter": "How we know"
    },
    {
      "id": "s24",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_spread",
      "narration": "With seismographs all over the world, scientists rebuild what's inside, like a giant ultrasound scan.",
      "on_screen_text": "An ultrasound of the planet",
      "highlight_words": [
        "ultrasound"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s25",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "and_globe",
      "narration": "And the point on the surface farthest from the center is in Ecuador: the summit of Chimborazo.",
      "on_screen_text": "Chimborazo, the farthest",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Chimborazo"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s26",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "mit_bulge",
      "narration": "That's because Earth, as it spins, bulges a little at the equator.",
      "on_screen_text": "A bulging Earth",
      "highlight_words": [
        "bulging"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s27",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "sub_row",
      "narration": "That's why volcanoes and earthquakes cluster along plate edges, like the Pacific coast.",
      "on_screen_text": "Along plate edges",
      "highlight_words": [
        "edges"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s28",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "dia_hard",
      "narration": "Diamond and the graphite in your pencil are the same carbon, just arranged differently.",
      "on_screen_text": "Pencil and diamond, same carbon",
      "highlight_words": [
        "carbon"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s29",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ima_moving",
      "narration": "And the magnetic north pole isn't fixed: it moves tens of kilometers every year.",
      "on_screen_text": "The pole moves",
      "highlight_words": [
        "moves"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s30",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ima_flip",
      "narration": "Over the planet's history, the magnetic poles have flipped many times.",
      "on_screen_text": "The poles flip",
      "highlight_words": [
        "flip"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s31",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_pacific",
      "narration": "Some earthquake waves can't pass through liquids. From the shadows they leave, we know the outer core is liquid.",
      "on_screen_text": "Shadows that reveal",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Shadows"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s32",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "and_cotopaxi",
      "narration": "That inner heat also powers volcanoes like Ecuador's Cotopaxi, almost six thousand meters high.",
      "on_screen_text": "Heat that drives volcanoes",
      "highlight_words": [
        "volcanoes"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s33",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "gal_plate",
      "narration": "The plate carrying the Galápagos moves a few centimeters a year, about as fast as your fingernails grow.",
      "on_screen_text": "As slow as your nails",
      "highlight_words": [
        "nails"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s34",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "dia_age",
      "narration": "Many diamonds are between one and three and a half billion years old: older than the dinosaurs.",
      "on_screen_text": "Older than the dinosaurs",
      "highlight_words": [
        "dinosaurs"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s35",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "aur_poles",
      "narration": "Without that magnetic shield, the solar wind would slowly wear away our atmosphere.",
      "on_screen_text": "A vital shield",
      "highlight_words": [
        "shield"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s36",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "mit_spin",
      "narration": "And all of it spins with you: at the equator you travel about a thousand six hundred kilometers per hour without noticing.",
      "on_screen_text": "Spinning without noticing",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Spinning"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s37",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "ima_core",
      "narration": "So under your feet there's rock, magma, diamonds and an iron heart hotter than any furnace.",
      "on_screen_text": "A living planet",
      "highlight_words": [
        "living"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s38",
      "role": "closing",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "and_outro",
      "narration": "How deep would you like to go? Tell me in the comments.",
      "on_screen_text": "How deep would you go?",
      "highlight_words": [
        "deep"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    }
  ],
  "description": "We go down layer by layer: the crust, the mantle where volcanoes and diamonds are born, the iron core that makes the magnetic field and a center as hot as the surface of the Sun. Original 3D animation; sizes and distances are not to scale.",
